  "text": "Mrs. Betselot Firdawok Debelle is an Ethiopian scholar, researcher, health advocate, project manager, and leadership trainer whose work bridges the worlds of public health, academia, and community development. Her unique perspective on the Omo Valley, the subject of this book, is shaped by a rare confluence of rigorous scholarship and a deeply personal connection. Born"
